CORE
packed_array_part_select3.sv
--bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.la\[1:0\] == 165: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.sa\[1:0\] == 165: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.sa\[1\]\.d == 3'b010: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p3\] always main\.la\[7:4\] == 0: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p4\] always main\.sa\[7:4\] == 0: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p5\] always main\.la\[0:-1\] == 80: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p6\] always main\.sa\[0:-1\] == 80: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p7\] always main\.la\[3:0\] == 165: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p8\] always main\.sa\[3:0\] == 165: PROVED up to bound 1$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A non-indexed part-select on a packed array whose range extends beyond the
array's declared range. The lowering extracted bits at a negative offset
(an invariant violation in the solver) or beyond the width of the flattened
array (a wrong value).
